# seed: 1
# requires: hero_ready scene_enter minigame_arm minigame_open minigame_slots_spin minigame_slots_result
# GAME 1 (Slobber Slots) at the Evergreen casino.
#
# WHERE THE CASINO IS, from the retail data and not from docs/gap_analysis.md (which says
# "scene 4" - scene 4 is an unreachable template; docs/re/script.md section 8 is right
# that the only real GAME opcodes live in the per-map scene files):
#     SCENE 1005  aztec                       extracted/worlds/Evergreen/QuestScenes1000.txt:93
#         THEME 0 / ACTOR 1 "Barker" / SEL 1 / MOVE 1,15,80
#         GAME 1                              QuestScenes1000.txt:99
#         ' Try your luck! / ' Our slots pay the most!
#         END
# Ten more identical casinos live in the same file, plus the SCENE 4 template at
# quest.txt:1720. The one that is actually on a map is reached from map 2:
#     map=2(castle1) link=3 x=264 y=267 kind=1 dest=0 target=1005 diff=1 theme=0 req=0 Casino
# and map 2 is Macgyver Castle, entered from map 0 link 9 "Macgyver Castle" at (151,275),
# which is 101 map units south-west of the Evergreen spawn at (179,202).
#
# `GAME n` opens nothing by itself. scene.c's OP_GAME is a comment worth repeating: it
# "does NOT block: FUN_00421529 arms the button, then pc++", so the opcode only arms a
# scene button-bar slot; the click is what opens the dialog. The armed slot is 6, the
# shared Shop/Equip/Game/Missions slot, at button_rect(6) = {640-51-51*6, 8, 48, 48} =
# {283,8,48,48}, centre (307,32) - scene.c:1287-1293 dispatches it, preferring
# missions, then the minigame, then the Equip panel.
# The slots window is RT_DIALOG 0xA7, 176x111, and scene.c:1536 renders it at (0,0), so
# the client rect of SPIN (control 0x447, DLU x=123 y=7 cx=46 cy=12) is the screen rect
# (123,7,46,12) and its centre is (146,13). The spin charges 10 GP (0x466BC6 refuses
# under 10) and settles by itself, which is what logs minigame_slots_result.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text Gambler
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
# The 101-unit walk, in three click legs inside the 82x71 map-unit view pane
# (19,0 325x281, four map units per screen pixel, hero hard-centred):
#   (179,202) -> (138,235) -> (151,270) -> (151,275) = map 0 link 9.
click 19 272
expect hero_move 900
click 235 280
expect hero_move 900
click 183 160
expect hero_move 900
expect map_enter 2000
# Map 2: the hero lands above map 2 link 0 "Main Gate" (158,333). The Casino link 3 is
# at (264,267); two legs east along y=267.
click 343 280
expect hero_move 1200
click 183 100
expect scene_enter 1200
shot /tmp/wos-gap-casino.bmp
# The armed GAME button, then the window's own SPIN control.
click 307 32
expect minigame_open 600
shot /tmp/wos-gap-slots-open.bmp
click 146 13
expect minigame_slots_spin 600
shot /tmp/wos-gap-slots-spin.bmp
expect minigame_slots_result 1500
shot /tmp/wos-gap-slots-result.bmp
quit
